{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1006883-mixed-dark-ages-multi-action-powers-whats-the-best-system","id":1006883,"title":"Mixed Dark Ages - multi-action powers.. whats the best system?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-22T15:27:31-08:00","id":1006883,"title":"Mixed Dark Ages - multi-action powers.. whats the best system?","content":"So my crew and I are thinking of a mixed-super (not very mixed really) Dark ages game. I'm intrigued by how DA:V20 has done celerity.<br /> <br /> Has any consideration gone into standardizing/streamlining multiple actions for all/other systems? How would we handle rage? Or pandemonium 5? Etc<br /> <br /> Looking for any ideas or canon rules that I may have missed. I don't see any other 20th anniversary dark ages game and I'm not sure they will come out at all actually","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4487-nerhesi","name":"Nerhesi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T18:13:54-08:00","id":1006943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nerhesi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1006883-mixed-dark-ages-multi-action-powers-whats-the-best-system#post1006883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So my crew and I are thinking of a mixed-super (not very mixed really) Dark ages game. I'm intrigued by how DA:V20 has done celerity.<br /> <br /> Has any consideration gone into standardizing/streamlining multiple actions for all/other systems? How would we handle rage? Or pandemonium 5? Etc<br /> <br /> Looking for any ideas or canon rules that I may have missed. I don't see any other 20th anniversary dark ages game and I'm not sure they will come out at all actually</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Kindred, Garou and Wraiths in one party? The first two isn't that unusual (well, in universe it is, but not in a gaming group), but the last seems an odd addition.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T21:24:07-08:00","id":1007022,"title":"","content":"Probably no wraiths - was just using that as an example. More likely, Kindred, Mages and Maybe a Garou.. Maybe. My question was more generalized so that regardless of what the group make up ends up as, what would be a good system to adopt.<br /> <br /> From my understanding, the DA:V20 system allows for more consistent use of multiple actions for all players - even though without celerity/rage/time/whatever. Have you folks experimented with Having Rage/2 (round down or up?) work similar to Celerity? Or any other system?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4487-nerhesi","name":"Nerhesi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T22:05:09-08:00","id":1007030,"title":"","content":"Balancing multiple actions isn't going to be your biggest problem. Unless your Kindred are 5th gens who were embraced in the Classical era or tutored unrealistically thouroughly by their sire, then you might want to look at you using Hedge Wizards instead of full blown mages. Other wise the Mage's are just going to be really over powered.<br /> <br /> Check out the <b>Sorcerer Revised Edition. </b>It's pretty awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T04:35:16-08:00","id":1007165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nerhesi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1006883-mixed-dark-ages-multi-action-powers-whats-the-best-system#post1006883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So my crew and I are thinking of a mixed-super (not very mixed really) Dark ages game. I'm intrigued by how DA:V20 has done celerity.<br /> <br /> Has any consideration gone into standardizing/streamlining multiple actions for all/other systems? How would we handle rage? Or pandemonium 5? Etc</div> </div> </div> </div>The power-idependant way of handling Multiple Actions *is* standardized in all the 20th books <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> &quot;Take lowest dice pool of all the actions, split that pool between actions.&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, except for one book. DA:V20. &quot;-1 die, +1 diff per action&quot;.<br /> That's the reason Celerity was handled so differently in that book.<br /> <br /> On one hand I personally highly prefer the way DA:V20 handles multiple actions, on the other hand I am annoyed that they, <b>yet again</b>, have not stuck to a single, uniform, in-every-damn-current-corebook standard that the other 20th books adhere to...<br /> <br /> Same reason I'm annoyed that all the 20th books use 'Expert knowledge' and 'professional skill' as a replacement for the old secondaries...except Mage 20th. Which uses secondaries again.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Oh yeah, my suggestion?<br /> Use the (Sadly not as good) Modern V20 multiple action and Celerity rules for your Vampires. That way you only have to adjust your DA vampires to the same system all the other books use, instead of having to come up with current DA rules for all the other gamelines..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 11-23-2016, 07:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T15:09:11-08:00","id":1007453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1006883-mixed-dark-ages-multi-action-powers-whats-the-best-system?p=1007165#post1007165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, my suggestion?<br /> Use the (Sadly not as good) Modern V20 multiple action and Celerity rules for your Vampires. That way you only have to adjust your DA vampires to the same system all the other books use, instead of having to come up with current DA rules for all the other gamelines..</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, this is about the best that can be come up with.<br /> Mages aren't too bad to work around, if you do away with (or otherwise mitigate) the ritual casting abuse. On the fly, their action actions are completely manageable. <br /> For Garou, Rage doesn't (usually) need to be modified, because it's such a small pool to work with. Garou having extra actions isn't as big of a hurdle as celerity (imo) because they only get a small number usually, and only for a round or 2.<br /> <br /> There is also the possibility of removing extra actions entirely. I've done it for at least one game and it makes things a lot more straight forward round-wise. But admittedly, there can be some work with figuring out how each splat interacts with that rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T16:12:26-08:00","id":1007478,"title":"","content":"Garou rage is an easy translation. Honestly though, Celerity gets rather nerfed in DA whilst rage can't take the same kind of hit (maybe multiple actions is limited to a third of your rage rather than half) Then again, Celerity gives dex dice, rage doesn't. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T05:35:18-08:00","id":1007671,"title":"","content":"Rage is already limited to your current Rage/2 number Rage points spent per turn. (Also i believe there was a limiter dependent on either Wits or Dex, can't remember which though).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T05:40:59-08:00","id":1007672,"title":"","content":"Rage is indeed limited by wits and dex. (you loose the need for wits in frenzy though). Thanks to celerity being crazy time magic, there is no such restriction there. <br /> <br /> However. Dark age celerity's multiple actions for attacks is halved, rounded up. <br /> 1-2 celerity is an extra attack<br /> 3-4 celerity is the third attack<br /> 5-6 celerity is the fourth attack. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile Rage. An Ahroun with nine rage gets 6 attacks a turn BEFORE taking dice pool penalties. <br /> <br /> <br /> It remains to be seen if the extra dexterity dice granted by celerity balances for this. (i think they can have a dodge action with celerity, the halfing is only for attacks if I recall)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T06:19:54-08:00","id":1007682,"title":"","content":"The extra attacks are unbalanced because WW never believed in allowing active defenses (unlike GURPS or Shadowrun). If they would just give people a defense pool that allowed them to protect against multiple attacks (or increased the required number of successes required as a simple way to represent an active defense), then they could balance the combat system and get rid of the declare action stage of the turn. Otherwise, offense always beats defense, and multiple attack combat monkeys always win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T09:14:13-08:00","id":1007735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1006883-mixed-dark-ages-multi-action-powers-whats-the-best-system?p=1007672#post1007672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Meanwhile Rage. An Ahroun with nine rage gets 6 attacks a turn BEFORE taking dice pool penalties.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ahroun (or really any Garou, Ahroun isn't a requirement) in this case can only take that many attacks is they've min/maxed to have a Dex and Wits to 5, and then only for 2 turns at most. After that they're spent, which is a decent limiting factor. Frenzy can free the Garou of the Wits restriction, but it still leaves Dex. And Frenzy comes with other drawbacks.<br /> A Vampire with Celerity 5 can do so at much less cost, depending on which edition you're using. Which is why (imo) Celerity needs to be nerfed if you are planning a crossover game. Though even for pure Vampire games, Celerity is far more powerful than the other physical Disciplines and generally needs to be nerfed every edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}